Package: catmech
Title: Auditable Sensitivity Completion with Interval Categories
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Patrick", "Iben", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "295464172+patrickiben@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Experimental sensitivity completion of a continuous measurement
    using trusted interval categories and quality flags. Combines constrained
    predictive mean matching, explicit retain-or-replace assumptions, strict
    input validation, and per-cell audit records. Provides objects compatible
    with 'mice' analysis tools. Does not identify latent truth, estimate
    corruption probabilities, or guarantee calibrated inferential intervals.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: digest, jsonlite, mice (>= 3.16.0), stats, truncnorm, utils, yaml
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), roxygen2, pkgload
Config/testthat/edition: 3
